// N6 — Shared capture: a function-local `var` mutated from inside a closure.
//
// The bytecode compiler promotes `total` to an `Arc<SharedCell>` (opcodes
// `AllocSharedLocal` / `LoadSharedLocal` / `StoreSharedLocal`), and the JIT
// mirrors that with an eager cell allocation at function entry. Before the fix
// this ABORTED the process (exit 134): `jit_alloc_shared_cell` had no
// `NativeKind` companion parameter (ADR-006 §2.7.8 / Q10 cell parallel-kind
// track) and was an unconditional `todo!()` — and because it is `extern "C"`
// (nounwind), the honest surface-and-stop manifested as a non-unwinding panic
// rather than a clean JIT bail.
//
// The mutation is observed through the OUTER scope's read of `total`, not the
// closure's return value: that is what proves the cell the JIT allocates in the
// declaring frame is the SAME cell the closure body writes through. A
// cell-identity mismatch would print 0 with exit 0 and no fallback line.
fn answer() -> int {
  var total = 0
  let bump = || { total = total + 42 }
  bump()
  total
}
print(answer())
